course: dictionary
lesson: 15387
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Spectacles has three meanings, and the sentence tells you which one is right. Most often it means glasses: the frame with lenses you wear to see better. Some people shorten it to specs.
explain: «Grandma put on her spectacles to read the menu.» You put glasses on to read, so spectacles here means glasses on her face.
explain: «The fireworks were a stunning spectacle over the bay.» Here a spectacle is a grand show that makes people stare in wonder. Spectacles is its plural, so «two spectacles» would mean two grand shows.
explain: «Tom made a spectacle of himself by dancing on the bus.» This phrase means he behaved in a silly way that made people stare. To check, try each meaning in the sentence: glasses or a grand show. Only the silly behaviour meaning makes sense.
fact: Spectacles means glasses: two lenses in a frame, worn to help you see better.
fact: Spectacles is a slightly old-fashioned word for glasses; in everyday talk people often say «specs».
fact: The lenses in spectacles bend light so that short-sighted or long-sighted people can see clearly.
fact: A spectacle is an impressive show or sight, like «a spectacle of fireworks». Spectacles is the plural of spectacle.
fact: «Make a spectacle of yourself» means to behave in a silly way that makes people stare.
exercise: «Grandma put on her spectacles to read the menu.» What are spectacles here? | A silly way of behaving | A grand firework show | *Glasses worn to help you see | A kind of hat
exercise: «The parade was a spectacle of bright costumes and music.» What does spectacle mean here? | A quiet, empty street | A mistake in a test | Glasses with thick lenses | *An impressive show
exercise: «Tom made a spectacle of himself by dancing on the bus.» What does this phrase mean? | Tom wore new glasses on the bus | Tom watched a show on the bus | *He behaved in a silly way that made people stare | He lost his glasses on the bus
test: Which meaning fits «Dad cleaned his spectacles before driving»? | Silly behaviour that makes people stare | Fireworks | Impressive shows | *Glasses
test: «The sunset over the sea was a spectacle nobody forgot.» What does spectacle mean? | Glasses | A silly act | A quiet corner | *An impressive sight
exam: «The science lesson showed how spectacles bend light.» What do spectacles mean here? | *Glasses with lenses | Lost property | A grand parade | Silly behaviour
